<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ussf-432 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 USSF-432 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 9.86 s, kick 3.589 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 16853 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.5333-0.001293*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
Not flown: SpaceX ussf432 page and LL2: Mon Nov 2 5:42 pm PST = 2026-11-03T01:42:00Z, 4 h window, backup Tue Nov 3 5:28 pm PST; booster 8th flight (LL2 B1095 -&gt; OCISLY). Checked 2026-10-31 ~8:30a PDT.
Published timeline (SpaceX ussf432): Max-Q 1:07, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:55, entry burn 6:06-6:30, landing burn 8:04, landing 8:26. SECO, orbit, deploy NOT published.
INFERRED/ASSUMED: SECO-1 time and parking orbit are a Starlink Group 15 analog (starlink-15-18), not USSF-432 sources. Azimuth from ZLA NOTAM hazard area. File ends 2 revs after cutoff (deploy unpublished).
Target (see launch config): insertion 177 km, apoapsis 266 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 153.56 deg; payload 16853 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-03T01:42:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (SpaceX publishes no SECO, restart or deploy time for USSF-432 (national-security payload); propagated 2 revs on the inferred (Group-15-analog) insertion orbit). From insertion T+519.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 88.93 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast.
POST-CUTOFF end T+11191 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 177.23 km, osculating 174.5 x 268.8 km, i 68.276 deg.</description>
